: \"The school board reached...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"concensus"},"2":{"Display":"consensus"},"3":{"Display":"consencus"},"4":{"Display":"consenssus"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID31","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"2","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID32","SecondaryAttribute":"Parts of Speech: In the sentence \"The surprisingly loud thunder frightened the children,\" what pa...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Parts of Speech:<\/b> In the sentence \"The surprisingly loud thunder frightened the children,\" what part of speech is the word surprisingly?","QuestionID":"QID32","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Parts of Speech: In the sentence \"The surprisingly loud thunder frightened the children,\" what pa...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Adjective"},"2":{"Display":"Noun"},"3":{"Display":"Adverb"},"4":{"Display":"Verb"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID32","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"3","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID33","SecondaryAttribute":"Transition Words: Choose the best transition word to complete the passage: \"The science fair was...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Transition Words: <\/b>Choose the best transition word to complete the passage: \"The science fair was a great success. ________, several students won scholarships for their projects.\"","QuestionID":"QID33","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Transition Words: Choose the best transition word to complete the passage: \"The science fair was...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Furthermore"},"2":{"Display":"Nevertheless"},"3":{"Display":"On the contrary"},"4":{"Display":"Meanwhile"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID33","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"1","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID34","SecondaryAttribute":"Scenario: Pre-writing. A student is staring at a blank piece of paper for an assignment titled \"M...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Scenario: <b>Pre-writing.<\/b> A student is staring at a blank piece of paper for an assignment titled \"My Hero.\" When asked, the student says, \"I don't have any heroes.\" What is the best instructional prompt?\n","QuestionID":"QID34","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Scenario: Pre-writing. A student is staring at a blank piece of paper for an assignment titled \"M...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Just write about Abraham Lincoln; he is an easy hero to write about."},"2":{"Display":"Let's brainstorm. Who is someone that helps you or that you look up to in your everyday life?"},"3":{"Display":"You have to write something or you will get a zero on this assignment."},"4":{"Display":"Look up the word 'hero' in the dictionary and copy the definition."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID34","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"2","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID35","SecondaryAttribute":"Scenario: Drafting. A first-grade student is writing a story but stops after every word to ask yo...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Scenario: <b>Drafting.<\/b> A first-grade student is writing a story but stops after every word to ask you how to spell it. How should the paraeducator respond to promote writing fluency?","QuestionID":"QID35","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Scenario: Drafting. A first-grade student is writing a story but stops after every word to ask yo...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Spell every word for them so the story is perfectly accurate."},"2":{"Display":"Tell them to write the sounds they hear and circle words they aren't sure about to fix later."},"3":{"Display":"Make them look up every single word in the dictionary before writing it down."},"4":{"Display":"Take the pencil and write the story for them as they dictate it."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID35","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"2","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID36","SecondaryAttribute":"Scenario: Revising vs. Editing. You are helping a student with the revising stage of a short stor...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Scenario: <b>Revising vs. Editing. <\/b>You are helping a student with the revising stage of a short story. Which of the following should you focus on?","QuestionID":"QID36","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Scenario: Revising vs. Editing. You are helping a student with the revising stage of a short stor...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Ensuring every sentence ends with the correct punctuation mark."},"2":{"Display":"Checking that all proper nouns are capitalized."},"3":{"Display":"Asking the student if their arguments make sense and if their paragraphs are in a logical order."},"4":{"Display":"Correcting all the misspelled words with a red pen."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID36","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"3","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID37","SecondaryAttribute":"Scenario: Supporting English Learners (EL). An EL student has great ideas for a paragraph about t...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Scenario: <b>Supporting English Learners (EL).<\/b> An EL student has great ideas for a paragraph about the water cycle but struggles to connect the sentences. What is the most appropriate scaffolding tool?","QuestionID":"QID37","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Scenario: Supporting English Learners (EL). An EL student has great ideas for a paragraph about t...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"A list of transition words and sentence frames."},"2":{"Display":"A lower-grade level coloring sheet about rain."},"3":{"Display":"Having the student write the paragraph in their native language instead."},"4":{"Display":"Telling the student to read the textbook again."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID37","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"1","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID38","SecondaryAttribute":"Scenario: Peer Review. Two students are doing a peer review, but one student simply wrote \"It is...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Scenario: <b>Peer Review.<\/b> Two students are doing a peer review, but one student simply wrote \"It is good\" on their partner's paper. How can you guide them to provide better feedback?","QuestionID":"QID38","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Scenario: Peer Review. Two students are doing a peer review, but one student simply wrote \"It is...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Tell the student that \"It is good\" is an unacceptable answer and give them a detention."},"2":{"Display":"Provide a simple checklist, asking them to identify one thing they liked and one thing that confused them."},"3":{"Display":"Do the peer review for them to show them how it is done."},"4":{"Display":"Tell the partner to ignore the feedback and just turn it in."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID38","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"2","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID39","SecondaryAttribute":"Scenario: Formulating a Topic Sentence. A second-grade student is writing an informative parapgra...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Scenario: <b>Formulating a Topic Sentence.<\/b> A second-grade student is writing an informative parapgraph about frogs. The current first sentence is: \"Frogs are a thing.\" How should the paraeducator assist?","QuestionID":"QID39","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Scenario: Formulating a Topic Sentence. A second-grade student is writing an informative parapgra...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Write a better topic sentence for the student to copy."},"2":{"Display":"Tell the student the sentence is fine and to move on to the body paragraphs."},"3":{"Display":"Ask guiding questions like, \"What kind of animal is a frog, and what is one interesting fact you learned about them?\" to help them make it more specific."},"4":{"Display":"Cross out the sentence and tell them to start over."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID39","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"3","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}]}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4","SecondaryAttribute":"A school is purchasing a new tablet that normally costs $300. The vendor offers a 20% educational...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"A school is purchasing a new tablet that normally costs $300. The vendor offers a 20% educational discount. What is the final price of the tablet?\n","QuestionID":"QID4","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"A school is purchasing a new tablet that normally costs $300. The vendor offers a 20% educational...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"$280"},"2":{"Display":"$260"},"3":{"Display":"$240"},"4":{"Display":"$60"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID4","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"3","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID40","SecondaryAttribute":"Scenario: Constructive Feedback. When pointing out errors on a student rough draft, what is the b...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Scenario: <b>Constructive Feedback.<\/b> When pointing out errors on a student rough draft, what is the best approach?","QuestionID":"QID40","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Scenario: Constructive Feedback. When pointing out errors on a student rough draft, what is the b...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Mark every single error on the page so the student knows exactly what they did wrong."},"2":{"Display":"Focus on one or two specific types of errors that align with the lesson objective."},"3":{"Display":"Only praise the student and ignore the errors to build self-esteem."},"4":{"Display":"Have another student correct the errors."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID40","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"2","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID41","SecondaryAttribute":"Scenario: Using a Rubric. The teacher has provided a 4-point rubric for a descriptive writing ass...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Scenario: <b>Using a Rubric.<\/b> The teacher has provided a 4-point rubric for a descriptive writing assignment. A student asks you if their paper is done. How should you respond?","QuestionID":"QID41","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Scenario: Using a Rubric. The teacher has provided a 4-point rubric for a descriptive writing ass...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Read the paper quickly and say, \"Yes, it looks good.\""},"2":{"Display":"Tell the student, \"Let's read through your paper together and compare it to the rubric requirements to see if you missed anything.\""},"3":{"Display":"Say, \"I am not the teacher, so I cannot tell you if it is done.\""},"4":{"Display":"Tell the student to keep writing until they fill up the entire page."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID41","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"2","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID42","SecondaryAttribute":"Read the passage: \"Inclusion is a model wherein students with special needs spend most or all of...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Read the passage: \"Inclusion is a model wherein students with special needs spend most or all of their time with non-disabled peers. Application of this model requires differentiated instruction, where teachers and paraprofessionals modify the delivery of content to meet varied learning profiles. While the primary goal is social and academic integration, implementation requires significant collaboration between general education and special education staff.\" <b>What is the primary requirement for a successful Inclusion model according to the passage?<\/b>","QuestionID":"QID42","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Read the passage: \"Inclusion is a model wherein students with special needs spend most or all of...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Separating students based on ability levels."},"2":{"Display":"Modifying how content is delivered to different students."},"3":{"Display":"Reducing the amount of time spent in the classroom."},"4":{"Display":"Hiring more administrative staff."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID42","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"2","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID43","SecondaryAttribute":"Based on the inclusion passage, the phrase \"learning profiles\" most likely refers to:","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Based on the inclusion passage, the phrase <b>\"learning profiles\"<\/b> most likely refers to:","QuestionID":"QID43","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Based on the inclusion passage, the phrase \"learning profiles\" most likely refers to:","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"A student physical appearance."},"2":{"Display":"A student historical grades."},"3":{"Display":"A student unique strengths, needs, and learning styles."},"4":{"Display":"A student disciplinary record."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID43","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"GradingData":[{"ChoiceID":"3","Grades":{"SC_4I7dsxjXjX6QtaC":"1"},"index":0}],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9nlqAiEPS5QQ7eC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID44","SecondaryAttribute":"According to the inclusion text, what is a necessary component for the implementation of inclusion?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"According to the inclusion text, <b>what is a necessary component for the implementation of inclusion?<\/b>","QuestionID":"QID44","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"According to the inclusion text, what is a necessary component for the implementation of inclusion?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Increased student testing."},"2":{"Display":"Teamwork between different departments."},"3":{"Display":"Standardizing all assignments."},"4":{"Display":"Decreasing the role of the paraprofessional."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"]